stdout Circuit: power-up / blanking sequence in the machine: the ~70 v, +18v and 6.8vac rails are up from t=0, +5v comes up through the tps54360b soft-start (2 ms ramp) at t=30 ms; blanking is an open-collector line from the cpu (2n3904, off during reset) pulled up by sr1 (4.7k) - it follows +5v up and stays high until the cpu releases it at t=200 ms. every latch is a 74hct574 that powers up with a random content (worst case: all 1) and is tri-stated while /oe (= blanking) is above vcc/2; below vcc = 2 v an hct output cannot drive. paths: solenoid (irlr3110z + ae-23-800 on 70 v), g.i. (mmbt4401 + bta16 macro + 6.8vac string), lamp column (tbd62083a with its internal pull-down, irfr5305 on +18v) with a row mosfet that happens to be on (74hct74 random state). at t=200 ms the cpu pulls blanking low with the latches still holding 1 -> the outputs must then turn on (the path works); at 240 ms the cpu writes 0.
